1
00:00:00,542 --> 00:00:04,998
Healthy routines break when the week changes, and generic
reminders don't explain why.

2
00:00:05,254 --> 00:00:13,655
In our simulator, with no support, members kept their routine on
63.7 percent of days, over 150 two-week episodes.

3
00:00:14,915 --> 00:00:19,050
Clinical Human Clone is for people keeping a routine going, and
the care team behind them.

4
00:00:19,302 --> 00:00:25,531
One sentence becomes a reviewed record, a passport that shows
where each value came from, and one bounded next step.

5
00:00:26,475 --> 00:00:27,229
Hypothesis:

6
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:34,554
a record the person confirms, plus a step matched to what drives
them, sustains a routine better than a fixed reminder, without
unsafe advice.

7
00:00:35,008 --> 00:00:35,481
Method:

8
00:00:35,853 --> 00:00:38,297
fixed rules run live, with no model call.

9
00:00:38,484 --> 00:00:41,733
Training and evaluation run offline, on synthetic members.

10
00:00:43,222 --> 00:00:44,177
The system checks itself.

11
00:00:44,752 --> 00:00:46,753
Nothing is saved until the person reviews it.

12
00:00:47,086 --> 00:00:49,491
A value older than 14 days is withheld.

13
00:00:49,742 --> 00:00:54,321
Every next step must pass versioned boundary rules, or it
becomes a hand-off to a person.

14
00:00:55,782 --> 00:00:58,025
This is the hosted prototype, recorded live.

15
00:00:58,439 --> 00:01:02,130
One synthetic sentence gives three values, each with its source
words.

16
00:01:02,705 --> 00:01:05,511
Sleep is corrected to six and a half hours, then saved.

17
00:01:09,482 --> 00:01:14,301
The passport traces each value through a five-step evidence
thread, from check-in to card.

18
00:01:14,675 --> 00:01:16,837
A card with no recent value is withheld.

19
00:01:19,349 --> 00:01:25,496
Inclinations show what weighs most for this member, from
simulated answers, and tie each next step to one of them.

20
00:01:27,249 --> 00:01:30,095
After a pain report, the next step routes to a person.

21
00:01:32,408 --> 00:01:34,450
Crisis language is never processed.

22
00:01:35,024 --> 00:01:37,791
A fixed hand-off appears, and nothing is saved.

23
00:01:38,922 --> 00:01:43,580
The research console reports every result with its run, its
split and its sample size.

24
00:01:45,908 --> 00:01:48,152
Results, all synthetic or simulated.

25
00:01:48,565 --> 00:01:53,545
On 141 held-out prompts, the base model passed the boundary
check 45 times;

26
00:01:53,919 --> 00:01:56,765
both trained stages passed all 141.

27
00:01:56,886 --> 00:02:05,689
Over 150 simulated episodes, the learned policy reached 0.840
mean adherence, against 0.833 for the best script.

28
00:02:06,988 --> 00:02:14,504
The boundary rules caught 74 of 74 labelled violations, with no
false alarms on 128 compliant rows.

29
00:02:14,709 --> 00:02:16,589
Our weakest result is lapse recovery:

30
00:02:17,084 --> 00:02:22,144
the trained replies pass that rubric on only 7 and 6 of 51
check-in prompts.

31
00:02:23,342 --> 00:02:25,262
What we expect, not yet measured:

32
00:02:25,636 --> 00:02:31,140
members who can see, correct and act on their record, and care
teams who see why a step was offered.

33
00:02:31,633 --> 00:02:35,084
The policy's edge over the best script is small, and simulated.

34
00:02:36,149 --> 00:02:36,741
The limits.

35
00:02:37,195 --> 00:02:40,968
No clinician has reviewed the content, and no person's health
data was used.

36
00:02:41,341 --> 00:02:44,429
Real input stays off behind 12 open governance gates.

37
00:02:44,883 --> 00:02:45,235
Next:

38
00:02:45,406 --> 00:02:48,575
a clinical reviewer, a consented pilot, and a measured result.

39
00:02:49,649 --> 00:02:52,857
Try the prototype and read the open-source code at the links on
screen.

40
00:02:53,432 --> 00:02:55,675
Clinical Human Clone, from Team Syntropy.
